{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"APPROVED portable design (a4, user-approved 2026-08-18). The ci-gate-compat verifier lens must NOT hard-code .github/workflows/** — that violates tech-agnosticism / project.portability. Instead:\n- Trigger via the DECLARATIVE applies_to glob seam in criteria_routing.json (the existing portable mechanism), covering multiple CI systems: **/.github/workflows/**, **/Jenkinsfile*, **/.gitlab-ci.yml, **/.circleci/**, **/azure-pipelines*.y*ml, **/.buildkite/**, **/bitbucket-pipelines.yml, **/.drone.yml. Adding a new CI system = adding a glob, not touching code.\n- Make the glob set project-overridable via a config key (e.g. [code_review] ci_config_globs) so an unusual pipeline is declared, not enumerated by us.\n- Phrase the verifier question CI-AGNOSTICALLY: 'Does this pipeline/gate-configuration change introduce a hard-fail step or required gate with no if-present/grandfather guard, so a branch created before this change would fail?' — no GitHub vocabulary in the prompt.\nMotivating grounded case: brattish-ladyish-jaguar (gate steps hard-fail on definition-vs-tree skew) — the pass-2 verifier could not reason about GH-Actions gate-step semantics; this criterion + a CI-agnostic lens is the finder/verifier fix."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787077843301739001,"uuid":"0b112bed-4fae-424e-a6ac-36454b44c96f"}